Close to Île aux Bénitiers, a lone rock rises from the turquoise shallows of the lagoon. The Crystal Rock is an exposed piece of fossilised coral reef, sculpted by the sea, and with the clear water around it and Le Morne in the distance it has become one of the most photographed places on the island.

Boats from La Gaulette and nearby villages stop here so that passengers can step into the shallow water around the rock.

## Good to know

- Go in the morning, when the water is calmest and clearest.
- Do not climb on the rock: it is fragile and slippery.
